// Regla Sigma: proc_creation_win_sysinternals_psexesvc_as_system.yml
// ID Sigma: 7c0dcd3d-acf8-4f71-9570-f448b0034f94
// Título: PsExec Service Child Process Execution as LOCAL SYSTEM
// Descripción: Detects suspicious launch of the PSEXESVC service on this system and a sub process run as LOCAL_SYSTEM (-s), which means that someone remotely started a command on this system running it with highest privileges and not only the privileges of the login user account (e.g. the administrator account)
// Aplica a: Producto: windows | Categoría: process_creation
// Producto: windows
// Categoría: process_creation
// Servicio: 
// Nivel: high
// Pipeline: microsoft_xdr
// Ruta original: C:\SigmaLab\sigma\rules\windows\process_creation\proc_creation_win_sysinternals_psexesvc_as_system.yml
// Requiere validación en el entorno de destino.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath =~ "C:\\Windows\\PSEXESVC.exe" and (AccountName contains "AUTHORI" or AccountName contains "AUTORI")
